  "why": "Pain on the outside of the elbow with gripping and lifting is lateral epicondylitis (\"tennis elbow\"): the tendon of the extensor carpi radialis brevis, where it starts on the lateral epicondyle, is the one most often involved. Most people who get it don't play tennis; repeated gripping and wrist work cause it. Flexor carpi radialis (D) is the trap: it starts on the medial epicondyle, the inside bump, and that is medial epicondylitis (\"golfer's elbow\").",
