  "why": "Stabbing pain under the heel with the first steps after sleep or rest, easing as you walk, is the classic sign of plantar fasciitis: the plantar fascia is the thick band under the foot from the heel bone to the toes, and it is sorest where it attaches to the heel. The Achilles tendon (C) is the trap: its pain is at the back of the heel or along the tendon above it, not underneath.",
