  "why": "A sudden sharp pain in the back of the thigh while sprinting is a hamstring strain, and the long head of the biceps femoris (on the outer side of the back of the thigh) is the hamstring most often strained in sprinting, typically as the leg swings forward late in the stride. Semitendinosus (A) is the trap: it's a hamstring too, one of the two inner hamstrings, but it's involved much less often.",
