  "why": "Hours of looking down at a phone tip the head forward, and the muscles at the back of the neck work harder to hold it; an aching side of the neck and top of the shoulder points to the upper trapezius, which runs from the base of the skull and the neck to the collarbone and shoulder blade (the levator scapulae often joins in). Supraspinatus (C) is the trap: it's part of the rotator cuff, and its pain is usually felt on the outside of the shoulder and upper arm, worse when lifting the arm, not up the neck.",
